+# Deterministic document automation (#741)
+
+Implementation status: the card and payroll source changes are locally
+checkpointed and independently source-reviewed. Batch tests, migration and
+rollback execution, browser checks, CI and publication remain pending. This page
+describes the implemented contract, not verified production readiness.
+
+## Upload and configuration
+
+An explicit manual PDF upload can request automatic processing. Extraction and
+eligibility use deterministic scripts; no AI or external OCR service is called.
+The retained original remains the source of evidence. Legacy callers that omit
+the automation request and scheduled source scans retain manual review.
+
+For cards, first upload a statement and explicitly map the recognized card to
+the selected account. Configure the counterpart, existing category rules and
+the intended scheduled payment, or explicitly choose no scheduled payment.
+An unset choice is distinct from choosing none. A masked hint never silently
+selects another account. New transactions require an unambiguous category rule;
+unknown categories are not guessed.
+
+For payroll, configure the salary account and employer/sender in the existing
+payslip settings. Automatic saving requires recognized wage sections, reconciled
+integer-cent totals and a supported payout date from the document or an eligible
+existing expectation. Unknown wage codes or conflicting records remain for
+review. Existing manually corrected payslips are not overwritten.
+
+## Financial outcomes
+
+- A supported, fully reconciled card statement can create eligible new purchase
+  bookings or link uniquely matching existing bookings. Same date and amount
+  alone do not prove a match. Ambiguous candidates remain under **Prüfen**.
+- Existing gross fuel purchases remain unchanged. A separately evidenced rebate
+  is a separate credit; a new purchase already entered at its discounted net
+  charge receives no second rebate.
+- Card settlement uses the issued statement's payable amount and explicit debit
+  date, never today's card balance. Consumer-card reconciliation requires the
+  corresponding previous source; supported company invoices have their own
+  subtotal, tax and total reconciliation. Missing source evidence remains
+  unresolved rather than becoming a balance correction.
+- A valid payroll document creates or links its exact payout through the existing
+  audited writer. Bank-account bookings remain pending until bank confirmation;
+  recording a document does not prove that the payment happened.
+- Results distinguish created records, existing links and unresolved portions.
+  Original documents and actual booking links remain available. No bank order,
+  message or external payment is sent.
+
+## Repeated uploads and corrections
+
+Source bytes, account configuration, captured revisions and current candidate
+records are checked again before financial writes. A repeated upload returns the
+existing result; it does not post the same money twice. Changed bytes for an
+existing source identity require review. Undo retains import history so that a
+retry does not silently recreate an undone financial action.
+
+Financial changes share an audit group and use the existing group Undo. Document
+review actions have their own document groups. Receipt links that support an
+active automatic result cannot be detached separately; undo the complete result
+first. Existing settlement and financial invariants continue to apply.
+
+## Storage and evidence boundaries
+
+The application's receipt store holds the authoritative original used for
+download and backup. Dropbox copies are an external archive and do not establish
+application links or reconciliation by themselves. These changes do not add a
+Gmail watcher or Dropbox synchronization service.
+
+The private extraction CLI remains read-only: it produces a proposal JSON and
+never posts financial records. See [statement intake](statement-intake.md) for
+storage, private extraction and backup details. The earlier summary-parser
+checks in that document do not validate the new transaction-row automation.
